<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Live sources are mostly cleartext: `http://` FLV, HLS over http, RTMP. Android
  9 (API 28) blocks cleartext by default, and the failure looks like a dead
  stream rather than a policy: the connection is refused before any bytes are
  read, so the player reports a network error and the recording never starts.

  A media host that plays what its users paste has to permit cleartext. The
  safer shape — a `<domain-config>` listing the hosts that need it — is not
  possible here, because the hosts are the rooms' own CDNs and change per
  deployment.

  This file is the example app's; an application copies it (and the two
  manifest attributes next to it) to get the same behaviour. See
  packages/media_core_recording_ffmpeg/README.md for the whole checklist.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
